<article class="env-lemma" id="09TE">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09TE">Lemma <span data-tag="09TE">37.58.9</span>.</a> Let $X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is locally of finite type. Let $\mathcal{F}, \mathcal{F}'$ be quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. If $\mathcal{F} \oplus \mathcal{F}'$ is finitely presented relative to $S$, then so are $\mathcal{F}$ and $\mathcal{F}'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Translation of the result of More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0672" data-tag="0672">15.82.10</a> into the language of schemes. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>